The workable formulation is a native Track-B graph task with two accepted witness encodings: an explicit permutation (so ordinary bipartite matching genuinely solves the posed problem) or a compact affine-XOR rule whose expansion is that permutation. The generator will plant the affine rule first, surround it with many statistically similar near-rules, and retain a connected graph by construction. This keeps the paper’s graph and vertex-map objects intact while making the planted rule short enough for the no-tool output caps.
