One final audit found another real grading risk: a solver could simply copy the syntactic example from the output instructions, and on a union of many matchings that example might accidentally verify. I’m adding “copy the example” as a sixth in-context attack, excluding it as the planted rule, and reserving an edge whenever the surrounding graph accidentally completes it.
