codex
Implemented the Track-B graph-derangement generator based on the paper’s native definition and Q-factor characterization ([arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.06286)).

Local verification passes:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Six attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Hopcroft–Karp reference: 8/8, averaging 10,769.75 edge scans.
- Compact answer: 51 characters, 7 atoms, 136 intended operations.
- Determinism and relabelling invariance verified.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.06286/gen_1507_06286.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.06286/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.06286/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.06286/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.06286/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.06286/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet externally hardened: all 12 official oracle calls returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`, leaving zero scored attempts. The error-only transcripts are preserved, and the README clearly marks `hard` as configured but not shippable until the OpenRouter quota is restored. I did not misclassify this infrastructure failure as a paper rejection.
